    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 9th with **Trea Turner** serving as our clear focal point. With a score of 79.92, **Trea Turner** is a must-start against Freeland; the synergy between his elite speed and the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery offers a high probability of stolen bases, which remains our primary focus given their scarcity. Supporting him in that same matchup is **Kyle Schwarber**, who maintains a strong 72.30 rating bolstered by his impressive 0.396 xwOBA and platoon advantage against the left-handed starter. We are also capitalizing on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.16) today; his dynamic platoon edge against Leiter and the favorable matchup against a pitcher with a slow delivery to the plate make him an underrated source of stolen base potential despite hitting in the bottom third of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation involved our bench depth versus the current starters. **Junior Caminero** and **Caleb Durbin** were immediate exclusions due to the rainout, keeping our focus strictly on active contests. Among available talent, **Chase Meidroth** (48.62) secured the final spot despite a marginal score, edging out other bench options because the wind blowing out at his venue provides a necessary ceiling-raising variable. Conversely, **Yordan Alvarez** (58.52) occupies a \"Strong\" start tier, though his score is slightly suppressed by a difficult assignment against the elite Burns; we continue to roster **Yordan Alvarez** for his elite 0.425 xwOBA, which consistently mitigates tough SP_xERA matchups. We are closely monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (47.24), whose score is being weighed down by a dynamic platoon disadvantage, but his role in the middle of the order keeps him marginally viable as we navigate a night where **Christian Yelich** remains on the IL and **Gary Sanchez** is out of the lineup entirely.",
